  "result": "Perfect! All 41 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`** \u2014 Added two new error codes:\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND`: That SKU is not on this invoice\n- `NOT_DRAFT`: Can only modify invoices with status draft\n\n**Added to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`**\n   - Adds a new line item to a draft invoice\n   - If SKU already exists, increases its qty instead\n   - Validates qty (QTY_INVALID) and SKU (UNKNOWN_SKU) like createInvoice\n   - Returns NOT_DRAFT if invoice.status isn't 'draft'\n   - Returns ok(newInvoice) with copied lines and products from catalogue\n\n2. **`removeLine(invoice, sku)`**\n   - Removes a line by SKU from a draft invoice\n   - Returns LINE_NOT_FOUND if SKU isn't on the invoice\n   - Returns NO_LINES if it would remove the last line\n   - Returns NOT_DRAFT if invoice.status isn't 'draft'\n   - Returns ok(newInvoice) without that line\n\nBoth functions:\n- Never mutate the input invoice or catalogue data\n- Return new objects with proper structure\n- Maintain immutability throughout\n\n**Added 13 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Adding new lines and updating existing SKUs\n- Validation of qty and SKU\n- Preventing modification of non-draft invoices\n- Immutability checks\n- Edge cases (removing last line, missing SKU)",
